{%- doc -%}
  One line inside a detail card (Figma: Standart Product Page → the three lines
  inside Estimated Shipping).

  A block rather than a pair of settings on the card above it, so a shop that also
  wants to state a cut-off time adds one and does not wait for a developer.

  This is the template's default only. A product that needs its own lines does not
  override them one at a time — it carries a list of `detail_row` metaobject
  entries, and [_ui-product-panel] draws those in place of these blocks.

  It renders [ui-detail-line] and adds nothing to it, so the look lives in the kit
  and the two paths cannot draw different markup.
{%- enddoc -%}

{% render 'ui-detail-line',
  label: block.settings.label,
  value: block.settings.value,
  attributes: block.shopify_attributes
%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Detail line",
  "tag": null,
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "label",
      "label": "t:settings.label",
      "default": "Ships from"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "value",
      "label": "Value",
      "default": "Made fresh, ships within 24 hrs"
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Detail line"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
